 om 11 AM to 4 PM Creative Hub Worcester becomes a FREE coworking commons i
 n Main South—created for anyone who needs a comfortable place to focus\,
  connect\, meet\, study\, or create. Bring your laptop\, schoolwork\, admi
 nistrative tasks\, creative project—or simply yourself. You’ll have ac
 cess to: ✨ Free Wi-Fi ❄️ Air conditioning 🪑 Plenty of open seatin
 g 🔇 Quiet rooms for meetings and video calls 🎨 A Makers Space for cr
 eativity and decompression ☕ A shared kitchen Come as you are. We’re c
 ommitted to providing a safe\, welcoming\, and affirming environment for p
 eople of all ages\, abilities\, backgrounds\, and identities. 📅 Thursda
 ys | 11 AM–4 PM 📍 Creative Hub Worcester 2 Ionic Ave.\, Worcester\, M
 A Registration Link: https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/co-working-thur
 sdays Registration is encouraged\, but drop-ins are always welcome!\n\nSou
 rces: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercent
 ralma.org/event/community-co-working-by-ponte-community-arts/30593/
LOCATION:Creative Hub Worcester\, 2 Ionic Avenue\, Worcester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/community-co-working-by-ponte-
 community-arts/30593/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CALL FOR ART! // WINTER LIGHTS\, SHARED STORIES EXHIBITION
DTSTART:20260817T000000
DTEND:20260930T000000
DTSTAMP:20260926T151138Z
UID:a7dd4d365bf0430b00fbbf8d4241f5@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:From the JMAC: Submission Details Deadline: September 30\, 202
 6 @11:59 PM EST -- The Hanover Theatre & Conservatory has a unique and sel
 ective visual arts opportunity for visual artists! We invite visual artist
 s to submit proposals for a series of window display installations that ce
 lebrate the spirit of gathering\, warmth\, and shared experience during th
 e winter season. These window display installations will be unveiled on De
 cember 17th\, the first day of the theater's winter festival! Artists may 
 incorporate seasonal or holiday-inspired imagery\, such as light\, ornamen
 tation\, or celebratory motifs\, so long as the overall concept remains we
 lcoming\, inclusive\, and not specific to one singular holiday or traditio
 n. ​ We are seeking proposals that interpret gathering and warmth in cre
 ative\, thoughtful\, and visually engaging ways. Concepts may include\, bu
 t are not limited to: - Connection\, community\, and togetherness - Light
 \, comfort\, and refuge during colder months - Shared rituals\, seasonal t
 raditions\, or moments of care - Abstract or symbolic representations of w
 armth and belonging CLICK HERE TO LEARN MORE\n\nSources: Discover Central 
 Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/call-fo
 r-art!-winter-lights-shared-stories-exhibition/30660/
LOCATION:Jean McDonough Arts Center\, 20 Franklin St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 0
 1608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/call-for-art!-winter-lights-sh
 ared-stories-exhibition/30660/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CALL FOR EXHIBITION PROPOSALS!
DTSTART:20260817T000000
DTEND:20260930T000000
DTSTAMP:20260926T151138Z
UID:2886d64cc53b120dd87b246fdc798b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:From the JMAC: Submission Details Deadline: September 30\, 202
 6 @11:59 PM EST -- We invite artists and curators to submit proposals for 
 a fully conceptualized exhibition to be presented in conjunction with thea
 trical performances of Hedwig and the Angry Inch\, performed and produced 
 by The Hanover Theatre Repertory in the BrickBox Theatre. This exhibition 
 will be presented in the gallery\, outside the theater\, creating a dynami
 c\, interdisciplinary experience that bridges visual art and performance. 
 Selected proposals should present a cohesive and immersive exhibition conc
 ept that responds to and engages with the central themes of Hedwig and the
  Angry Inch. Artists are encouraged to interpret these themes broadly and 
 creatively. ​Thematic Focus Proposals must be rooted in themes inspired 
 by Hedwig and the Angry Inch\, including but not limited to: - Identity an
 d self-discovery - Transformation and reinvention - Gender\, queerness\, a
 nd fluidity - Love\, loss\, and longing - The body as a site of fragmentat
 ion and wholeness - Fame\, performance\, and persona - Resilience\, surviv
 al\, and personal mythology -- CLICK HERE TO LEARN MORE\n\nSources: Discov
 er Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/ev
 ent/call-for-exhibition-proposals!/30662/
LOCATION:Jean McDonough Arts Center\, 20 Franklin St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 0
 1608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/call-for-exhibition-proposals!
 /30662/
END:VEVENT
