BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sasha Velour: Travesty
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260926T000000
DTSTAMP:20260926T151138Z
UID:4ef47406c96875825584c1d41654b4@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Travesty traces the secret queer history of a single spot thro
 ughout time — A witch burns in a field\; a clown builds a theater\; an u
 nderground gay bar rises up against the police. As Velour embodies differe
 nt characters through a series of jaw-dropping lip-syncs\, she invites you
  to take part in the cycle of existence\, resistance and camp that IS drag
 . Part performance art\, part history\, part call to action\, Travesty wil
 l have you screaming at the top of your lungs\, dancing in the aisles and 
 inspired to “change the muthaf*ckin’ world!” “Beyond its status as
  a top-tier drag show\, it is point blank one of the most outstanding perf
 ormances presently on stage.” – BroadwayWorld “‘Travesty’ was no
 t just a drag show\, it was a queer seance\, a visual rebellion\, and a lo
 ve letter to the ghosts history tried to erase.” – Queerland Media Vel
 our is known for her unique fusion of lip sync performance\, video art\, a
 nd storytelling. She is the winner of Season 9 of RuPaul’s Drag Race (20
 17)\, the founder and host of New York City’s legendary drag revue Night
 Gowns (since 2015) and has toured two celebrated one-queen theater shows a
 round the world—Smoke & Mirrors (2019-2022)\, and The Big Reveal (2023-2
 025).\n\nSources: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.
 discovercentralma.org/event/sasha-velour%3a-travesty/30665/
LOCATION:The Hanover Theatre and Conservatory for the Performing Arts\, 2 
 Southbridge St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/sasha-velour%3a-travesty/30665
 /
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sen. Raphael Warnock Comes to Worcester: Sept. 26 & 27 2026
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260926T151138Z
UID:c5fb66b2141735b0815c1a04e42b83@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:DCU Center in Worcester\, MA U.S. Senator and Senior Pastor of
  the Historic Ebenezer Baptist Church in Atlanta\, Georgia is known as a p
 rophetic voice at the intersection of faith and justice. Since 2005\, Rev.
  Dr. Warnock has served as the Senior Pastor of the Historic Ebenezer Bapt
 ist Church in Atlanta\, Georgia - spiritual home of the Rev. Dr. Martin Lu
 ther King\, Jr. He became the first African American elected to the United
  States Senate from the state of Georgia in 2021\, and is a prominent voic
 e advocating for expanded healthcare access\, voting rights\, and criminal
  justice reform. Warnock has spent his career dedicated to bettering the l
 ives of others\, from the pulpit and from the Senate floor alike\, a voice
  at the intersection of faith and justice that continues to inspire a gene
 ration reaching for moral clarity and bold action. Dr. Warnock is known fo
 r viewing his religious tradition as a bridge rather than a weapon\, cente
 red on love and human dignity. He teaches that true faith requires caring 
 for the hungry\, the sick\, and the stranger rather than enacting policies
  that hurt low-income families. Tickets to his address on Sept. 26 are $35
  to attend in person or to watch the livestream - ​Purchase below. Sen. 
 Warnock will be signing books following his address. Rev. Warnock will als
 o preach at worship on Sunday\, Sept. 27 at 10:00 AM at the DCU Center. Al
 l are welcome free of charge\, but must register here.\n\nSources: Discove
 r Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/eve
 nt/sen-raphael-warnock-comes-to-worcester%3a-sept-26-%26-27-2026/30770/
LOCATION:DCU Center - Arena and Convention Center\, 50 Foster Street\, Wor
 cester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/sen-raphael-warnock-comes-to-w
 orcester%3a-sept-26-%26-27-2026/30770/
END:VEVENT
