BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The NAA invites you to the 25th Annual Art Auction Exhibition & Ev
 ent
DTSTART:20260926T110000
DTEND:20261028T170000
DTSTAMP:20260926T151138Z
UID:dd49f198508626ced9143f5d622b54@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) invites artists\, members\, collectors\,
  friends\, and art lovers to gather for a celestial celebration of 25 year
 s of creativity\, connection\, and community. This year’s Art Auction ex
 hibition is on display from Wednesday\, September 2nd until Saturday\, Oct
 ober 3rd. A ticketed auction party will be held on Saturday\, October 3rd
 \, from 4-8pm. Over 160 artworks are available for online silent auction b
 idding now until October 3rd @6pm. In the downstairs Sargent Gallery\, the
  exhibit includes NAA Member Artwork featuring photography\, mixed media\,
  sculpture\, oil\, acrylic and more. Upstairs in the Hartson Gallery is th
 e Collector’s Collection – showcasing artwork donated from private col
 lections\, including work by notable artists such as Harold Feinstein\, Ca
 ra Weston\, and Carlos Mérida. For online bidding & tickets to our Octobe
 r 3rd party\, visit: Auctria.events./NewburyportArt25 Since 1948\, Newbury
 port Art has believed in the power of art to bring people together. For on
 e unforgettable event\, Saturday\, October 3rd\, from 4-8pm\, 65 Water Str
 eet will transform into a celebratory theme of a black\, white and silver 
 sky. The afternoon and evening offers a variety of ways to experience the 
 celebration including: live painting by Alan Bull and a chance to purchase
  his piece\; bidding on Members’ Artwork\, Collectors Collection\, and S
 ilent Auction Packages\; adding your own star and to an interactive commun
 ity constellation\; free tarot reading\; dancing to live jazz & swing with
  Jared Holaday\; sipping on a signature cocktail from the open bar\; enjoy
 ing catered food and dessert\; posing for your Moon Portrait in the sculpt
 ure garden\; and sharing your NAA story in an optional two-minute video in
 terview. NAA Member tickets: $70\; Non-member tickets: $90\; with a sugges
 ted attire of cosmic shine! Thank you to our lead sponsors\, Matter Commun
 ications\, Milestone 35 Tools & Woodworking\, and the Hylton Family Trust 
 for supporting our 25th Annual Art Auction. Gallery Hours: Wednesday throu
 gh Sunday from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More 
 information\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.
 org.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/ev
 ent/the-naa-invites-you-to-the-25th-annual-art-auction-exhibition-event/20
 26-09-26/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/the-naa-invites-you-to-the-25th-annual
 -art-auction-exhibition-event/2026-09-26/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Wild & Tended" with Mary Mackenzie\, soprano and Matthew Jaskot\,
  piano
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260926T000000
DTSTAMP:20260926T151138Z
UID:f1b7b79ee9acd177e67330607088cb@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Art song was born as an intimate genre\, written to be perform
 ed in people’s homes — music for a room\, for a gathered circle of fri
 ends\, for a voice close enough to hear every detail. It continues to be a
  vibrant and diverse genre\, and this program lives in that tension — be
 tween the wild and the tended — tracing art song from its Romantic roots
  to music written in our own time. Featuring an array of songs by Clara Sc
 humann\, Hugo Wolf\, Arnold Schoenberg\, Lili Boulanger\, Francis Poulenc
 \, and American composers Charles Ives\, Aaron Copland\, Samuel Barber\, a
 nd John Frantzen. All events are free to those under 18. The Massachusetts
  Card To Culture covers all holders of a current EBT\, WIC\, or Commonweal
 th Connector Care Insurance card. Click on links for each card for more ge
 neral information about this program. Card holders may request up to two f
 ree tickets at the box office for any ticketed concert on the concert day
 \, or may make a reservation by email to events@friendsofthestonechurch.or
 g. Please include your name\, an email address or telephone number\, conce
 rt date and # of tickets being reserved in your request. About the Artists
  Critically acclaimed as “a soprano of extraordinary agility and concent
 ration” by The New York Times \, soprano Mary Mackenzie has emerged as o
 ne of contemporary music’s most compelling storytellers. With a career t
 hat has taken her to performances in 11 U.S. States and Washington D.C.\, 
 as well as a seasoned discography spanning eleven years\, Ms. Mackenzie is
  particularly known for her evocative chamber music performances. For her 
 efforts\, she has earned praise for a “sensational\, epically unsettling
 ” rendition of George Crumb by the Boston Globe and her “mystifying”
  vocal effects by The Financial Times . Examples of some of her most immer
 sive work to date includes several “one-woman” performances\, like the
  United States premiere of Héctor Parra’s monodrama H ypermusic: Ascens
 ion at the Guggenheim Museum\, a highly technological experience which uti
 lized Harvard professor of theoretical physics Lisa Randall as librettist.
  www.marymacksoprano.com Matthew Jaskot is a composer\, pianist\, organist
 \, concert curator\, and a professor of music at the College of the Holy C
 ross in Worcester\, MA where he teaches music theory\, composition\, and i
 s the collaborative pianist for the College Choir. Matt is a versatile pia
 nist who specializes in 20th and 21st century music\, while being equally 
 adept at performing traditional repertoire\, jazz\, and popular music. He 
 has performed nationally and internationally at various festivals and conf
 erences\, most recently as guest performer in the Ecce Ensemble\, premieri
 ng works at the Etchings Festival in Northampton\, MA. Last spring\, he or
 ganized a program\, featuring a two-piano performance of Stravinsky's Le S
 acre du Printemps\, with colleague Sonya Ovrutsky Fensome\, a collaborativ
 e concert with the dance department at Holy Cross. www.matthewjaskot.com\n
 \nSources: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discove
 rcentralma.org/event/wild-%26-tended-with-mary-mackenzie-soprano-and-matth
 ew-jaskot-piano/30856/
LOCATION:Stone Church Cultural Center\, 283 Main Street\, Route 32\, Gilbe
 rtville\, MA\, 01031
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/wild-%26-tended-with-mary-mack
 enzie-soprano-and-matthew-jaskot-piano/30856/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Worcester Chamber Music Society Concert: Autumn Winds - Worcester
DTSTART:20260926T000000
DTEND:20260926T000000
DTSTAMP:20260926T151138Z
UID:4ce9647b6b1a6d608dcfabe7b8ab70@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Autumn Winds We open the season with three pieces written in t
 hree centuries. Mozart and Brahms each composed works in their masterful s
 tyles that display the virtuosity of the hornist and clarinetist for whom 
 they were written. Dohnányi’s Sextet showcases both instruments in a wo
 rk that nods to Brahms while delighting in its own eccentricity and sass. 
 Saturday\, September 26 @7:30 PM Jeanne Y. Curtis Hall* Assumption Univers
 ity 500 Salisbury Street\, Worcester *located in the Tsotis Family Academi
 c Center Pre-concert talk @7:00 PM Program Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart: Horn Q
 uintet in E-flat major\, K.407/386c Johannes Brahms: Clarinet Trio\, Op. 1
 14 Ernő Dohnányi: Sextet\, Op. 37 With guests Gary Gorczyca\, clarinet /
  Clark Matthews\, horn venue is handicapped accessible\n\nSources: Discove
 r Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/eve
 nt/worcester-chamber-music-society-concert%3a-autumn-winds-worcester/30758
 /
LOCATION:Worcester Chamber Music Society\, 500 Salisbury Street Tsotis Fam
 ily Academic Center Assumption University\, Worcester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/worcester-chamber-music-societ
 y-concert%3a-autumn-winds-worcester/30758/
END:VEVENT
