BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nashoba Valley Pride (Rescheduled)
DTSTART:20260927T000000
DTEND:20260927T000000
DTSTAMP:20260926T151138Z
UID:62c3cca18f3f022458bae043c87dc2@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate community\, inclusion\, and Pride at the 2026 Nashob
 a Valley Pride Celebration\, a free\, family- and kid-friendly event hoste
 d by the Nashoba Valley Pride Committee. This annual celebration brings to
 gether LGBTQ+ individuals\, families\, friends\, neighbors\, and allies fr
 om across the Nashoba Valley and beyond for an afternoon of connection\, v
 isibility\, education\, entertainment\, and fun in the heart of Bolton\, M
 assachusetts. The day begins with a community Pride Parade at 1:00 PM\, de
 parting from Emerson School\, traveling along Main Street\, and concluding
  at the Bolton Town Common\, where the Pride Festival continues until 4:00
  PM. Festival attendees can enjoy an exciting lineup of speakers\, drag pe
 rformances\, live music\, community organizations\, local vendors\, raffle
 s\, and a variety of food trucks. Visitors will also have the opportunity 
 to connect with LGBTQ+ organizations and local community groups that provi
 de education\, resources\, advocacy\, and support throughout the region. W
 hether you're attending with children\, meeting friends\, or simply lookin
 g to show your support as an ally\, Nashoba Valley Pride offers a welcomin
 g and inclusive atmosphere where everyone is encouraged to celebrate authe
 nticity\, respect\, and belonging. The event is free and open to the publi
 c. Schedule 1:00 PM: Pride Parade from Emerson School to the Bolton Town C
 ommon 1:30–4:00 PM: Festival on the Bolton Town Common Festival Highligh
 ts Community Pride Parade Inspiring speakers Drag performances Live music 
 LGBTQ+ organizations and community resources Local vendors Food trucks Raf
 fles Family-friendly activities and community celebration Parking Parking 
 is available at: Emerson School Florence Sawyer School First Parish Church
 \, 673 Main Street The event is ADA accessible. Follow @nashobavalleypride
  on Facebook and Instagram for updates\, announcements\, and additional ev
 ent information. More info is also available at https://tinyurl.com/nvpf20
 26. Come celebrate a vibrant\, welcoming community where everyone belongs!
 \n\nSources: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.disco
 vercentralma.org/event/nashoba-valley-pride-(rescheduled)/30461/
LOCATION:Bolton Town Common\, Bolton MA\, 100 Powdermill Road Suite 159\, 
 Acton\, MA\, 01720
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/nashoba-valley-pride-(reschedu
 led)/30461/
END:VEVENT
