SUMMARY:Summer\, 1976
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTSTAMP:20260926T151138Z
UID:3728c965f14b97136f382f9e768612@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Summer\, 1976 is a deeply affecting two-hander by Pulitzer Pri
 ze–winning playwright David Auburn\, whose celebrated body of work inclu
 des Proof and other acclaimed plays that examine intellect\, memory and th
 e fragile complexities of human connection. A longtime artistic presence a
 t Berkshire Theatre Group\, Auburn has written and directed multiple produ
 ctions on BTG stages\, bringing both his precision as a playwright and his
  emotional clarity as a director to the company’s work. In Summer\, 1976
 \, he turns his focus to an unexpected friendship between two women whose 
 lives intersect during the Bicentennial summer. What begins as a brief enc
 ounter unfolds into a quietly transformative bond\, leaving an imprint tha
 t shapes both women for decades to come.\n\nSources: The Berkshires\nEvent
  page: https://berkshires.org/events-old/summer-1976/
LOCATION:Unicorn Theatre\, 6 East Street\, Stockbridge\, MA\, 01262
URL:https://berkshires.org/events-old/summer-1976/
END:VEVENT
